# ADR-004: Host the Site on Amazon ECS

## Status: Accepted (Date: October 26 2026)

## Context
ADR-001 moved the site from static hosting to a server-rendered docker container. The application needs a container runtime on AWS. Hosting supports replacing unhealthy tasks and deploying new versions without interrupting the site.

## Decision
The container will run on Amazon ECS using Fargate. GitHub Actions will
run the unit tests, build the Docker image, push it to Amazon ECR, and deploy the updated task definition to the ECS service.

## Alternatives considered
Amazon EC2: Provides control over the host, but requires managing and
  the underlying instances.
Amazon EKS: Provides Kubernetes orchestration, but adds operational
  complexity that is not needed for this application.

## Consequences
Positive: Fargate runs containers without requiring managing host
  instances.
Positive: ECS health checks and task replacement can help keep the service
  available when a task becomes unhealthy.
Negative: The service incurs compute costs, and needs IAM permissions configured